%N A038216 Triangle whose (i,j)-th entry is binomial(i,j)*2^(i-j)*10^j.
%H A038216 Björg N. Cyvín, Jon Brunvoll, and Sven J. Cyvín, <a href="https://match.pmf.kg.ac.rs/electronic_versions/Match34/match34_109-121.pdf">Isomer enumeration of unbranched catacondensed polygonal systems with pentagons and heptagons</a>, Match, No. 34 (Oct 1996), 109-121.
%F A038216 T(n,k) = 10*T(n-1,k-1) + 2*T(n-1,k) with T(0,0)=1, T(n,k)=0 for k<0 or k>n. - _Ranjan Kumar Dhani_, Oct 08 2026
%e A038216 The triangle begins as:
%e A038216   1;
%e A038216   2,  10;
%e A038216   4,  40,  100;
%e A038216   8, 120,  600,  1000;
%e A038216  16, 320, 2400,  8000,  10000;
%e A038216  32, 800, 8000, 40000, 100000, 100000;
%e A038216  ...
%t A038216 Table[Binomial[i,j]2^(i-j) 10^j,{i,0,10},{j,0,i}]//Flatten (* _Harvey P. Dale_, Dec 05 2021 *)
